					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-5728973#post-3768596</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-5728973/scp-2128046979-j#post-3768596</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 14 Apr 2018 01:34:08 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>A Random Day</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1841781</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Manti Te'o's girlfriend as a joke SCP is a format that has been used a couple times already with varying degrees of success, such as <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3999-j">SCP-3999-J</a> and SCP-007-J; however, I daresay that the former's success was primarily due to being a parody of 3999 and the latter's to having a reasonably funny dialogue.</p> <p>I think this would work a lot better if it really leaned into the joke, possibly by tying into the Antimemetics Division or the general prevalence of amnestics - ideally, using the joke to skewer one of the various memory-related story concepts on the site in general.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
